---
// Where a heavy validation actually runs: one host-wide counting semaphore,
// exact-identity coalescing ahead of it, and the verdict record every gate
// reads afterwards. Shipped half on the left (docs/WORKTREES.md "Host-wide
// admission", docs/VALIDATION-RECORDS.md). The right half is direction: an
// external CI handler returning a typed result that lands in the same ledger.
// The typed result protocol itself (beadhive-validation-result/v1) ships and
// is opt-in; remote execution does not.
---
<figure id="fig-validation-slots">
  <div class="diagram">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1160 520" role="img"
      aria-label="Left, shipped: four validation requests from three worktrees arrive at one host-wide semaphore with one slot. The first submit is admitted and executes; a second submit of the same hive, tree and command coalesces behind it and consumes its verdict without a slot; a check and a merge wait in the queue. Attest keys run under the admitted gate's permit. The execution writes a run manifest and a verdict pointer keyed by tree and command hash, which submit, merge, finish, the push hook and release preflight all read. Right, direction: an external CI handler runs the same command remotely, writes the typed result protocol file, and the verdict lands in the same ledger so the same gates and hooks consume it; cross-host trust needs a signing story first.">
      <defs>
        <marker id="vs-n" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="var(--ink-3)"/></marker>
        <marker id="vs-h" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="var(--honey)"/></marker>
        <marker id="vs-g" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="var(--green)"/></marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- ===== host ===== -->
      <rect class="lane-i" x="16" y="16" width="716" height="488" rx="10"/>
      <text class="lane-label" x="32" y="38">ONE HOST — SHIPPED · work.validation_slots: 1 · BH_VALIDATION_SLOTS wins</text>

      <!-- requesters -->
      <text class="d-kicker" x="32" y="70">REQUESTS</text>
      {[
        { y: 96,  cmd: 'bh work submit bh-api-7',  id: 'hive api · tree T1 · cmd H', note: 'leader — admitted', cls: 'd-box-h' },
        { y: 166, cmd: 'bh work submit bh-api-7',  id: 'hive api · tree T1 · cmd H', note: 'same identity — follower', cls: 'd-box-g' },
        { y: 236, cmd: 'bh work check bh-web-3',   id: 'hive web · tree T7 · cmd H', note: 'queued for a slot', cls: 'd-chip' },
        { y: 306, cmd: 'bh work merge bh-api-9',   id: 'hive api · tree T9 · cmd H', note: 'queued for a slot', cls: 'd-chip' },
      ].map((r) => (
        <g>
          <rect class={r.cls} x="32" y={r.y - 22} width="226" height="54" rx="6"/>
          <text class="d-code" x="44" y={r.y - 4}>{r.cmd}</text>
          <text class="d-mute" x="44" y={r.y + 11}>{r.id}</text>
          <text class="d-mute" x="44" y={r.y + 25}>{r.note}</text>
        </g>
      ))}

      <!-- identity lock: follower -> leader -->
      <path class="flow-g" d="M 258 166 C 290 166, 290 110, 262 100" marker-end="url(#vs-g)"/>
      <text class="d-mute" x="300" y="138">identity lock (hive, tree, cmd_hash):</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="300" y="152">serializes ahead of admission — the follower</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="300" y="166">takes no slot, consumes the leader's verdict</text>

      <!-- semaphore -->
      <rect class="d-box" x="300" y="196" width="190" height="196" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="314" y="218">host semaphore</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="314" y="234">one heavyweight gate at a time</text>
      <rect class="d-box-h" x="314" y="246" width="162" height="60" rx="6"/>
      <text class="d-code-h" x="324" y="264">slot 0 · executing</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="324" y="278">bh-api-7 · clean checkout of T1</text>
      <rect class="d-chip" x="324" y="286" width="60" height="14" rx="3"/><text class="d-mute" x="354" y="297" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:9px">key: unit</text>
      <rect class="d-chip" x="390" y="286" width="78" height="14" rx="3"/><text class="d-mute" x="429" y="297" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:9px">key: stateful</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="314" y="326">attest keys run under the parent's</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="314" y="340">permit — no extra slot</text>
      <rect class="d-chip" x="314" y="350" width="162" height="30" rx="6"/>
      <text class="d-code" x="324" y="363">queue · bh-web-3, bh-api-9</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="324" y="375">queue_seconds recorded per run</text>

      <path class="flow-h" d="M 258 96 C 280 96, 280 262, 310 262" marker-end="url(#vs-h)"/>
      <path class="flow" d="M 258 236 C 280 236, 280 360, 310 360" marker-end="url(#vs-n)"/>
      <path class="flow" d="M 258 306 C 280 306, 280 366, 310 366" marker-end="url(#vs-n)"/>

      <!-- records -->
      <path class="flow-h" d="M 490 276 H 526" marker-end="url(#vs-h)"/>
      <rect class="d-box" x="530" y="196" width="186" height="104" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="544" y="218">the record</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="544" y="236">.bh/validation/runs/&lt;run-id&gt;/</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="544" y="250">manifest · reports/ · gate.log</text>
      <text class="d-code-g" x="544" y="272">verdicts/&lt;tree&gt;/&lt;cmd_hash&gt;</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="544" y="286">green · red · none · uses/</text>

      <path class="flow-g" d="M 623 300 V 330" marker-end="url(#vs-g)"/>
      <rect class="d-box-g" x="530" y="334" width="186" height="90" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="544" y="354">who reads it</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="544" y="370">submit · merge · finish · union</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="544" y="384">the push-main hook</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="544" y="398">release preflight · attest</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="544" y="412">exact (tree, cmd_hash) · TTL P1D</text>

      <text class="d-mute" x="32" y="420">0 slots disables admission — reserve it for a separately contained CI host.</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="32" y="436">Slots are host policy, not per-hive: a hive-local value is ignored.</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="32" y="452">bh work check seeds the same store, so check → submit at one sha pays once.</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="32" y="468">A dead owner is marked abandoned; its locks release and one follower takes over.</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="32" y="484">Lower priority for the gate: work.validation_priority (nice / ionice).</text>

      <!-- ===== external handler (direction) ===== -->
      <rect class="d-box-dir" x="748" y="16" width="396" height="488" rx="10"/>
      <text class="lane-label" x="764" y="38">EXTERNAL CI HANDLER</text>
      <rect class="d-chip-dir" x="938" y="26" width="120" height="16" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-mute" x="998" y="38" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:9.5px">direction</text>

      <rect class="d-chip" x="764" y="70" width="364" height="54" rx="6"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="778" y="90">the same command, run elsewhere</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="778" y="106">a CI engine or another frame takes the (tree, cmd) and the</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="778" y="118">host's slot stays free — the handoff is the unbuilt part</text>

      <path class="flow dashed" d="M 946 124 V 150" marker-end="url(#vs-n)"/>
      <rect class="d-box-g" x="764" y="154" width="364" height="88" rx="6"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="778" y="174">typed result — shipped, opt-in</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="778" y="192" style="font-size:9.2px">work.validation_protocol: beadhive-validation-result/v1</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="778" y="206">bh exports BH_VALIDATION_RESULT_PATH; the trusted runner writes</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="778" y="220">{`{"verdict": "green|red|none", "reason": …}`}</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="778" y="234">green with a nonzero exit is rejected — never less than red</text>

      <path class="flow-g dashed" d="M 946 242 V 268" marker-end="url(#vs-g)"/>
      <rect class="d-chip" x="764" y="272" width="364" height="70" rx="6"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="778" y="292">lands as an attestation, not a special case</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="778" y="308">same verdict key (tree, cmd_hash), same per-key states,</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="778" y="322">so the same gates and the same push hook consume it</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="778" y="336">with no new bypass added</text>
      <path class="flow-g dashed" d="M 764 306 C 740 306, 740 272, 718 272" marker-end="url(#vs-g)"/>

      <rect class="d-box-r" x="764" y="364" width="364" height="60" rx="6"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="778" y="384">what has to be decided first</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="778" y="400">a verdict from another host is a trust claim, not a cache:</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="778" y="414">it needs signing (ADR Decision 6 — out of scope in v1)</text>

      <rect class="d-chip-dir" x="764" y="438" width="364" height="54" rx="6"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="778" y="458">validation broker — proposal</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="778" y="474">resource-aware queue: declared CPU / memory / named pools,</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="778" y="486">priority and measured runtime; pueue vs HyperQueue bake-off</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Admission is a host question, not a hive question: one counting semaphore covers
  every worktree on the machine, defaulting to a single heavyweight gate at a time, and exact
  concurrent requests for the same <code>(hive, tree, command)</code> serialize ahead of it so a
  duplicate submit never spends a slot. What comes out is a durable run record plus a verdict
  pointer keyed on the tree and command hash — the object every later boundary reads. The
  right-hand half is the shape an offload would take: the runner protocol already lets a trusted
  external runner return a typed verdict, and because that verdict is just another attestation
  under the same key, the gates and the pre-push hook would need no new code path. What is not
  built is the handoff itself, and what is not decided is how a verdict earned on another machine
  is trusted.</figcaption>
</figure>
